1
00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,796
Every enterprise has a system nobody dares to touch.

2
00:00:03,796 --> 00:00:07,562
A mainframe ledger. A warehouse batch file from 1994.

3
00:00:07,562 --> 00:00:09,623
A scan of a printed manifest.

4
00:00:09,623 --> 00:00:13,745
The data inside is quietly rotting, and no one can see it.

5
00:00:13,745 --> 00:00:16,090
NecroLegacy performs the autopsy.

6
00:00:17,796 --> 00:00:22,578
Drop in a legacy dump, a COBOL copybook, or a photo of a printed table.

7
00:00:22,578 --> 00:00:27,562
Three synthetic presets are built in, so you can try it with no real data.

8
00:00:38,987 --> 00:00:41,009
Five agents run in a fixed order.

9
00:00:41,009 --> 00:00:45,911
The schema archaeologist infers entities, keys and relationships from raw bytes.

10
00:00:45,911 --> 00:00:50,690
Deterministic checks and an isolation forest score the rot before any language

11
00:00:50,690 --> 00:00:55,225
model is involved. The model only explains what the numbers already found.

12
00:01:03,555 --> 00:01:06,248
The verdict arrives like a coroner's notice.

13
00:01:06,248 --> 00:01:09,980
Orphaned foreign keys and negative stock are always critical.

14
00:01:09,980 --> 00:01:14,019
Healthy specimens glow steadily, and the rotten ones glow crimson.

15
00:01:14,019 --> 00:01:17,140
Drag to orbit, open any specimen for its anomalies,

16
00:01:17,140 --> 00:01:21,179
and every interaction has a keyboard and screen reader equivalent.

17
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:26,276
Search the records in plain words, and the broken ones surface.

18
00:01:26,276 --> 00:01:30,739
Then the last agent resurrects the system: a typed FastAPI wrapper,

19
00:01:30,739 --> 00:01:33,203
syntax checked and ready to download.

20
00:01:34,105 --> 00:01:35,452
It reads paper too.

21
00:01:35,452 --> 00:01:40,343
Drop in a faded dot-matrix manifest, and the first pass runs locally.

22
00:02:10,555 --> 00:02:14,695
In the Vision X-Ray, confident regions are green, while smudged,

23
00:02:14,695 --> 00:02:19,869
torn or faded cells are crimson, so nothing unreadable is passed off as certain.

24
00:02:20,770 --> 00:02:23,068
NecroLegacy was built with Kiro.

25
00:02:23,068 --> 00:02:27,161
A 19-requirement spec drove the design and the task list,

26
00:02:27,161 --> 00:02:30,752
steering files kept every agent on the same rules,

27
00:02:30,752 --> 00:02:35,778
and an MCP server lets Kiro inspect a legacy schema and query its rot.

28
00:02:35,778 --> 00:02:39,369
Live today on Cloud Run, Render, Neon and Upstash.

29
00:02:39,369 --> 00:02:41,523
NecroLegacy. Autopsy the past.

30
00:02:41,523 --> 00:02:42,672
Ship the future.
